D2DX 0.99.529: the motion prediction steps at most 40 ms (one game tick) per frame.

D2DX predicts where units, texts and weather particles are between the game's
ticks and moves them by velocity times the time of the last frame. That time had
no upper bound: after a long frame (the device stalled for a second) a rain drop
was moved up to 2500 px, and its stretched quad overflowed the 16-bit vertex
positions. White lines (one, or two crossing) ran across the picture for that
frame. Now the frame time is stored as at most 40 ms; a longer frame only shows
the movement of one tick. The app ships the glide3x.dll of the D2DX 0.99.529
release with the HRESULT fix (d2dx-0.99.529-comexception-hresult.patch) and
this change in two places, applied by tools/binpatch.py (patch
"d2dx-glide3x-frametime") when the assets are fetched:

  file      glide3x.dll
  before    sha256 5c4997371d9ca183bd7f0b17bc2f33eb9193f85e34cd94cc7153127b68bc5725
  after     sha256 c4edd7b6d2b64373ff6f2f8b7d04437a41b14e57b582d7542f09ec1407ae6f89
  change    file offset 0x5336: cc cc cc cc cc cc cc cc cc cc cc cc cc cc cc cc cc cc cc cc cc cc -> b8 28 00 00 00 f2 0f 2a c8 f2 0f 5d c1 f2 0f 11 87 08 01 00 00 c3
            (int3 padding after a function at 0x10005f36: mov eax, 40; cvtsi2sd xmm1, eax;
            minsd xmm0, xmm1; movsd [edi+0x108], xmm0; ret)
  change    file offset 0x99cf: 0f 57 c9 f2 0f 5a c0 f3 0f 5a c8 0f 28 c1 f2 0f 5c 87 00 01 00 00 f2 0f 11 8f 00 01 00 00 f2 0f 11 87 08 01 00 00 -> f2 0f 5a c0 f3 0f 5a c8 0f 28 c1 f2 0f 5c 87 00 01 00 00 f2 0f 11 8f 00 01 00 00 e8 47 b9 ff ff 66 0f 1f 44 00 00
            (RenderContext::Present at 0x1000a5cf: the same computation without the
            dead "xorps xmm1, xmm1", and "call 0x10005f36" in place of the store of
            _frameTimeMs; a 6-byte nop keeps the length. Both places use no absolute
            addresses, so no relocation is involved.)

The source change it corresponds to:

--- a/src/d2dx/RenderContext.cpp
+++ b/src/d2dx/RenderContext.cpp
@@ -469,7 +469,7 @@
 	}
 
 	double curTime = TimeEndMs(_timeStart);
-	_frameTimeMs = curTime - _prevTime;
+	_frameTimeMs = min(curTime - _prevTime, 40.0);
 	_prevTime = curTime;
 
 	if (_deviceContext1)
